# Imports & Types

## Path alias

Always use `@/` for imports (maps to `./src/`):

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD
import { beatService } from "@/lib/services/beat.service";
import BeatCard from "@/components/BeatCard";

// ❌ BAD
import { beatService } from "../../../lib/services/beat.service";
```

## Import order

1. External packages (`react`, `next`, `mongoose`, `zod`, `lucide-react`)
2. Internal libraries (`@/lib/...`)
3. Components (`@/components/...`, `@/features/...`)
4. Types (`@/types`, type-only imports)
5. Relative imports (`./SomeClient`)

## Type definitions

- Domain interfaces live in `src/types/index.ts` with `I` prefix: `IBeat`, `IUser`, `IOrder`.
- Zod-inferred types in validators: `CreateBeatInput`, `BeatFilterInput`.
- UI types in feature files: `BeatPackUi` in `src/features/beats/beat-pack-ui.ts`.
- Use `type` imports for type-only: `import type { Metadata } from "next"`.
